# `x: T` / `p: *T` parameter and no struct carrier carries rides the first parameter declared `*..*T` (`_pp_tparam`,
# d stars), and the struct its whole argument points through to binds it (`_tok_pp_arg`). The scan answered 0, so
# `var r = gd2(&GPP); r.pick(t)` in a generic left `r` untyped, the forward of T into the stub method `P_pick` was not
# seen, and the generic's i64 base was refused naming `P.pick`, where the parser binds `gd2`'s T to P. CHANGELOG [6.7.16]
