# ⛔ 6.7.15 — THE TOKEN BINDING FOLLOWS THE PARSER'S POINTER RULE (6.7.14's D8 (a), `_ic_arg`): the whole argument at
# token at, through fi's carrying parameter — `p: *T` (`ptr` 1) or `x: T` — read as the parser binds it, from the
# tokens. It read only a name or a whole call, the same through both shapes, so `var r = gd(&G); r.pick(t)` in a
# generic was refused naming the stub method (the scan left `r` untyped: `gd(&G)` answered 0, so the forward of T into
# `P_pick` was not seen and the generic's base was not a stub), as was a `var p: *P` local's `gd(p)`; and a
# `pp: *S` PARAMETER answered S through `x: T`, where the parser binds no pointer. Through `p: *T`: `&name` of a struct
# value (`_tok_ta_addr`), a name declared `*S` or a struct value, a field chain whose leaf is declared `*S`
# (`_tok_ta_chain`), a call returning a struct or `*S` (`_tok_ta_call`); through `x: T`: a struct value, a whole
# dereference `*p` of a name declared `*S` (6.7.15's D12 (a)), a call returning a struct; either, inside a whole-
# argument wrap (D12). Anything else answers 0 — a missed flag, never a false one. CHANGELOG [6.7.15]
# 6.7.15 (D23 A): through `p: *T`, pointer arithmetic on one of those pointers too (`_tok_ta_arith`), as the parser
# binds it (`_ic_parith`).
# ⛔ 6.7.17 (D2): a whole field or method chain on any receiver head, from the unit's tokens (`_acv_bind`), as the
